orcshot (0.1.0-21) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix the editor window overflowing the screen vertically on Wayland
    when the capture is taller than what's available - live-confirmed
    on the Ubuntu 26.04 Wayland VM (direflail, 2026-08-22) with a
    diagnostic trace showing self.resize() to an already screen-
    clamped size was itself being overridden - the window grew *past*
    even its own requested target (804x768 requested, 856x857 actual),
    not just failing to shrink to it. The same scenario already
    clamped correctly on X11. Fixed with Gtk.Window.set_geometry_hints
    (MAX_SIZE) - a protocol-level constraint that maps directly to
    Wayland's own xdg-shell set_max_size(), which the compositor is
    required to respect during its own size negotiation, unlike GTK's
    internal widget-tree sizing which resize() alone didn't fully
    constrain here. Verified live on the same VM across both an
    oversized and a normal-sized capture - the window now correctly
    stays within the screen's work area in both cases, with no
    regression on X11 (verified locally, unchanged).

