orcshot (0.1.0-19) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix the intermittent jump left over after 0.1.0-18's fix - real
    journalctl evidence (direflail, 2026-08-22) caught it directly: on
    some editor opens, the window correctly appeared at
    Gtk.WindowPosition.CENTER's own placement, then visibly jumped to
    the work area's top-left corner a moment later. Root cause,
    confirmed with a direct, repeated live test: self.get_position(),
    called from the same idle_add timing _resize_canvas_and_window
    uses, is genuinely racy against the window's own real
    configure-event - it returned a stale (0,0) in 4 of 5 live runs,
    before the real, CENTER-placed position had actually been
    reported back yet. The position-clamp logic added earlier today
    trusted that stale read and explicitly moved the window there,
    intermittently overwriting CENTER's own already-correct placement
    - exactly matching the "still has issue intermittently" report.
    Now tracks position from the configure-event itself (never stale,
    it's the geometry that just genuinely happened) instead of
    querying it fresh, and skips repositioning entirely on the very
    first call, before any real position is known yet, rather than
    guess. Verified live across 8 repeated runs, including the exact
    racy case - no more stale-position moves, in either case the
    window settles correctly.

 -- Orcshot <314918217+artificialorctelligence@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:15:00 -0500

orcshot (0.1.0-18) noble; urgency=medium

  * Editor window placement, round 4 - direflail correctly pushed back
    that "we never had this issue before today" (2026-08-22): three
    earlier attempts this session (removing Gtk.WindowPosition.CENTER,
    then an explicit move() to the primary monitor, then no position
    hint at all) were chasing the wrong hypothesis, based on an
    artificial test that didn't reflect real usage. Direct, decisive
    comparison using the diagnostic logging added this session (same
    window, same session, only the position hint changed): *without*
    CENTER, Cinnamon/Muffin's placement-mode=automatic policy runs its
    own multi-step negotiation for a brand-new window with no position
    request at all - a real, visible sequence of position changes
    before it settles, occasionally onto a different monitor. *With*
    CENTER restored, the same window settles in one step and stays
    there. Restored it - this is likely the real, original explanation
    for the very first report of this bug too, not a wrong-monitor
    problem. The self-correcting configure-event handler and
    Greenshot-faithful "clamp position to stay on-screen, don't force
    dead-center" resize logic from earlier today are kept as
    defense-in-depth. Diagnostic logging is kept for one more round
    pending live confirmation this is actually resolved, not stripped
    prematurely.

