orcshot (0.1.0-17) noble; urgency=medium

  * Editor window placement, round 3 (direflail, 2026-08-22): the
    cross-monitor jump is gone (0.1.0-16's configure-event fix), but a
    smaller same-monitor jump remained - the editor's post-capture
    resize used to always recenter dead-center on its monitor. Checked
    what real Windows Greenshot does (ImageEditorForm.cs): it never
    recenters at all, only ever sets Size - WinForms grows from the
    form's existing top-left corner, Location untouched. The editor
    now does the same: grows in place from wherever the window manager
    already put it, only nudging position enough to stay fully
    on-screen if growing would otherwise push it past the work area's
    edge, rather than unconditionally jumping to geometric center.
    Also adds temporary WARNING-level diagnostic logging to every
    configure-event and resize/move decision (visible via `journalctl
    --user -u orcshot.service`, no logging config needed) - direflail's
    own ask, since isolated reproduction scripts keep failing to
    replicate the real, mouse/window-manager-timing-sensitive
    behavior; this gets a real trace from the next live repro instead
    of more guessing. Will be removed once whatever's left is fully
    nailed down.

