orcshot (0.1.0-5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix save_image_to_file always building an RGBA (has_alpha=True)
    pixbuf regardless of target format. JPEG has no alpha channel -
    Ubuntu 24.04's older GdkPixbuf JPEG backend silently discarded it,
    but 26.04's newer glycin-based one rejects an RGBA-flagged pixbuf
    outright ("does not support the color type Rgba8"). Confirmed as
    the real cause of 0.1.0-4's resolute build failure via the actual
    Launchpad buildlog. save_image_to_file now composites onto white
    and builds a genuine 3-channel, has_alpha=False pixbuf for JPEG
    specifically.

